From 6885456aa178e0dff2fca3faa5c3378392cab49e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:08:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(motion): the plain 3D finish hop never goes below the
 run end

The plain hop of emit_runs took its travel plane from the retract
plane and the next run start only. With a retract plane below the end
of the current run (a cavity with Contour, or a convex part cut inner
first), the tool fed down into the part at the run end and made a
rapid through it. The verifier held the post (envelope gouge 3 mm,
rapid in stock), so nothing passed silently.

The hop plane is now never below the run end. The move across is made
at that plane only if the plane is over every facet or the exact sweep
(gaplink::straight_ok) clears it; else the hop goes to clearance. With
a retract plane at or above the model top the hop is unchanged.

Fixes #3627

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
